es render artifacts, and you consume them if they exist.\n\n\n/workspace/agents/developer.md:\n  Line 110: rendered result with the `shot` tool instead of reasoning from code alone:\n\n  Line 112: - `shot <url>` — render + measure a URL at 1280×900 (PNG + render report to\n\n  Line 113:   `screenshots/` in the job dir)\n\n  Line 114: - `shot <url> --widths 375,768,1280` — responsive review\n\n  Line 115: - `shot <url> --full-page` — full-height capture\n\n  Line 116: - `shot <url> --describe` — vision-model prose (works where `ZHIPU_API_KEY`\n\n  Line 123: commit (screenshot hygiene). Read-only agents never run `shot`; they consume\n\n  Line 127: cannot), run `shot <url> --describe` and reason from the prose — the vision\n\n  Line 128: layer turns the screenshot into design-relevant text. Correct in both cases:\n\n\n/workspace/agents/quality.md:\n  Line 135: When a job's render report exists (`screenshots/render-report.md` + PNGs in the\n\n  Line 137: they are ground truth for what the UI actually looks like. Never run `shot`\n\n\n/workspace/agents/owner.md:\n  Line 89: You are a read-only agent: never run `shot`. If a job's render report\n\n  Line 90: (`screenshots/render-report.md` + PNGs in the job dir) exists, read it for\n\n\n/workspace/skills/webapp-testing/PROVENANCE.md:\n  Line 15:     `pip install playwright` (network egress available). Upstream assumes\n\n\n/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md:\n  Line 128: one-shot shortcut that registers the current directory and suggests its base\n\n  Line 184: The `shot` tool (`/usr/local/bin/shot`, see the manigot README's PLAYWRIGHT\n\n\n/workspace/skills/webapp-testing/SKILL.md:\n  Line 3: description: Toolkit for interacting with and testing local web applications using Playwright. Supports verifying frontend functionality, debugging UI behavior, capturing browser screenshots, and viewing browser logs.\n\n  Line 12: `import playwright` fails, install the client with\n\n\n(Results truncated. Consider using a more specific path