rsal,\n33:   session-wide* constraints (they apply to every agent, not just the\n34:   developer), not as a restatement of the developer prompt. If a rule cannot\n35:   be made meaningfully broader than an existing prompt/skill, flag it in\n36:   `implementation.md` rather than inventing scope.\n37: - The brief's `~70 more` skills and manigot's `internal/session/policies.go` /\n38:   `AGENTS.md` are not present in this repository, so the dedupe check in\n39:   TASK-6 is limited to the files that actually exist here.\n40: \n41: ## Task breakdown\n42: \n43: ### TASK-1 — Author `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n44: \n45: - **Description**: Create the global policy file forbidding committing,\n46:   logging, printing or hardcoding secrets, tokens, keys or credentials\n47:   (read them from env/config instead), written as a short universal\n48:   always/never rule per the brief's format.\n49: - **Files**: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` (new)\n50: - **Depends**: none\n51: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file, no code paths or other artifacts\n52:   affected.\n53: \n54: ### TASK-2 — Author `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n55: \n56: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no debug\n57:   output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO (without a tracked\n58:   issue) be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n59: - **Files**: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` (new)\n60: - **Depends**: none\n61: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n62: \n63: ### TASK-3 — Author `policies/smallest-change.md`\n64: \n65: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring the smallest change\n66:   that satisfies the task (no refactoring or tidying of adjacent code, no scope\n67:   expansion), framed as a session-wide constraint rather than a developer-only\n68:   instruction.\n69: - **Files**: `policies/smallest-change.md` (new)\n70: - **Depends**: none\n71: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; the only judgement call is wording to\n72:   avoid merely restating `agents/developer.md` (noted above).\n73: \n74: ### TASK-4 — Author `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n75: \n76: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring explicit approval\n77:   before adding a dependency, framed universally for all sessions/agents.\n78: - **Files**: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` (new)\n79: - **Depends**: none\n80: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; overlaps slightly with the developer\n81:   prompt, so wording must add the session-wide framing.\n82: \n83: ### TASK-5 — Author `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n84: \n85: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no uncommitted\n86:   work be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n87: - **Files**: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` (new)\n88: - **Depends**: none\n89: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n90: \n91: ### TASK-6 — Audit the new `policies/` set against the brief's criteria\n92: \n93: - **Description**: Compare all files under `policies/` against the brief's four\n94:   decision criteria and the existing catalog content that actually exists here\n95:   (`prompts/*.md`, `agents/*.md`, `skills/`); trim wording, or drop a file\n96:   entirely, if it is not universal, is longer than a short rule, restates a\n97:   skill or a core agent prompt with no added scope, or is situational — and\n98:   record any such decision in `implementation.md`.\n99: - **Files**: `policies/*.md` (may be edited or, if a file fails the criteria,\n100:   removed); `implementation.md` (note the outcome)\n101: - **Depends**: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n102: - **Risk**: medium — this is a judgement-based pass that can change or reduce\n103:   the delivered set, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n104:   brief's criteria.\n105: \n106: ## Notes / open questions\n107: \n108: - The brief leaves the exact set open (\"names/content are a starting\n109:   suggestion\"). These tasks author all five proposed policies and rely on\n110:   TASK-6 to enforce the criteria; if a policy fails, the brief's intent is to\n111:   drop it, so the final set may be fewer than five. This is treated as in\n112:   scope, not a scope expansion.\n113: - No human decision was required to produce this breakdown.\n\n(End of file - total 113 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: policies\n\nid: medical\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\nsmall set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\nplain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\nthe four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\nreal spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n\nScope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n  `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: policies\n\nid: medical\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\nsmall set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\nplain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\nthe four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\nreal spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n\nScope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n  `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the\n  brief says keep the directory to policy files only (the catalog scan ignores\n  those, but the brief is explicit).\n- Every file must be short: a one-line heading + the rule + at most a line or\n  two of why. If a rule needs more than that, it belongs in a skill, not here.\n\nNotes for @developer (not blockers):\n- The repo contains no build or test tooling; verification is content review\n  against the brief's criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n- The brief is explicit that names/content are a starting suggestion. Several\n  proposed rules (`smallest-change`, `ask-before-adding-dependencies`,\n  `keep-it-committed`) overlap with existing core agent instructions\n  (`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/developer.md`). Author them as *universal,\n  session-wide* constraints (they apply to every agent, not just the\n  developer), not as a restatement of the developer prompt. If a rule cannot\n  be made meaningfully broader than an existing prompt/skill, flag it in\n  `implementation.md` rather than inventing scope.\n- The brief's `~70 more` skills and manigot's `internal/session/policies.go` /\n  `AGENTS.md` are not present in this repository, so the dedupe check in\n  TASK-6 is limited to the files that actually exist here.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n### TASK-1 — Author `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file forbidding committing,\n  logging, printing or hardcoding secrets, tokens, keys or credentials\n  (read them from env/config instead), written as a short universal\n  always/never rule per the brief's format.\n- **Files**: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file, no code paths or other artifacts\n  affected.\n\n### TASK-2 — Author `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no debug\n  output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO (without a tracked\n  issue) be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n- **Files**: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n\n### TASK-3 — Author `policies/smallest-change.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring the smallest change\n  that satisfies the task (no refactoring or tidying of adjacent code, no scope\n  expansion), framed as a session-wide constraint rather than a developer-only\n  instruction.\n- **Files**: `policies/smallest-change.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; the only judgement call is wording to\n  avoid merely restating `agents/developer.md` (noted above).\n\n### TASK-4 — Author `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring explicit approval\n  before adding a dependency, framed universally for all sessions/agents.\n- **Files**: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; overlaps slightly with the developer\n  prompt, so wording must add the session-wide framing.\n\n### TASK-5 — Author `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no uncommitted\n  work be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n- **Files**: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n\n### TASK-6 — Audit the new `policies/` set against the brief's criteria\n\n- **Description**: Compare all files under `policies/` against the brief's four\n  decision criteria and the existing catalog content that actually exists here\n  (`prompts/*.md`, `agents/*.md`, `skills/`); trim wording, or drop a file\n  entirely, if it is not universal, is longer than a short rule, restates a\n  skill or a core agent prompt with no added scope, or is situational — and\n  record any such decision in `implementation.md`.\n- **Files**: `policies/*.md` (may be edited or, if a file fails the criteria,\n  removed); `implementation.md` (note the outcome)\n- **Depends**: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n- **Risk**: medium — this is a judgement-based pass that can change or reduce\n  the delivered set, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n  brief's criteria.\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- The brief leaves the exact set open (\"names/content are a starting\n  suggestion\"). These tasks author all five proposed policies and rely on\n  TASK-6 to enforce the criteria; if a policy fails, the brief's intent is to\n  drop it, so the final set may be fewer than five. This is treated as in\n  scope, not a scope expansion.\n- No human decision was required to produce this breakdown.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":113,"totalLines":113,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791733802274,"end":1791733802373}},"id":"prt_12ba82506001OWZTMJQ13sG3nx","sessionID":"ses_ed458233dffes0Lk4CTNEuavw6","messageID":"msg_12ba81c0d001sfTuZ2T3k7PgwR"}}
