{"type":"text","timestamp":1791733935929,"sessionID":"ses_ed458233dffes0Lk4CTNEuavw6","part":{"id":"prt_12baa1890001HuQmR8IiyIo9Tc","messageID":"msg_12baa12fe001SlQFa8tv4Z8RHr","sessionID":"ses_ed458233dffes0Lk4CTNEuavw6","type":"text","text":"Both tasks are complete and the worktree is clean.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Job:** `prior` — new policy: playwright only if necessary\n\n**TASK-1 — Authored `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md` (committed `d1aef59`)**\n- New global catalog policy, plain markdown, no frontmatter, filename-as-identity — following the format established by the `medical_policies` job (heading + rule + a line of why, 5 lines total, matching the shape of the four existing policy files).\n- Framed around the universal principle per the analyst's recommended resolution: prefer static analysis / reading the code / lighter tests over browser automation; reach for Playwright (or a `shot` render) only when those cannot answer the question. Playwright is named as the motivating example, not the whole subject; the heading states the universal rule.\n\n**TASK-2 — Audited against catalog (committed `1757ce2`)**\n- Verified universal (not situational), short, adds scope rather than restating:\n  - `prompts/meta.md` encourages verification but does not ration *which* path — no restatement, no contradiction.\n  - `agents/developer.md`'s `shot` UI-verification guidance stays intact: for rendered UI, static analysis can't answer, so `shot` remains correct; the policy only rules out browser runs where a cheaper check suffices.\n  - `agents/tester.md:50/96` already carries \"not everything needs a browser\" as a role-scoped bullet — promoting it to an always-on rule is added scope (same reasoning that kept `no-debug-leftovers`).\n  - No overlap with `webapp-testing`/`frontend-design` skills or the other four policies.\n- Wording kept as delivered; all reasoning recorded in `implementation.md`.\n\n**Deliverables:** `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md` (new), `implementation.md` (filled in with summary, per-task changes, and known issues — including the noted follow-up that softening `agents/developer.md`'s unconditional \"verify UI with shot\" wording would be a separate job). Worktree is clean; no pushes, no merges, nothing outside `/workspace` touched.","time":{"start":1791733930129,"end":1791733935921}}}
