{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791734038276,"sessionID":"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_61d20ba5d86f48da81ccb8cd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: policies\n2: \n3: id: medical\n4: analyst: analyst\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n8: \n9: ## Overview\n10: \n11: Add a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\n12: small set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\n13: plain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\n14: the four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\n15: real spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n16: \n17: Scope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n18: - Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n19:   `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n20: - Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the\n21:   brief says keep the directory to policy files only (the catalog scan ignores\n22:   those, but the brief is explicit).\n23: - Every file must be short: a one-line heading + the rule + at most a line or\n24:   two of why. If a rule needs more than that, it belongs in a skill, not here.\n25: \n26: Notes for @developer (not blockers):\n27: - The repo contains no build or test tooling; verification is content review\n28:   against the brief's criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n29: - The brief is explicit that names/content are a starting suggestion. Several\n30:   proposed rules (`smallest-change`, `ask-before-adding-dependencies`,\n31:   `keep-it-committed`) overlap with existing core agent instructions\n32:   (`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/developer.md`). Author them as *universal,\n33:   session-wide* constraints (they apply to every agent, not just the\n34:   developer), not as a restatement of the developer prompt. If a rule cannot\n35:   be made meaningfully broader than an existing prompt/skill, flag it in\n36:   `implementation.md` rather than inventing scope.\n37: - The brief's `~70 more` skills and manigot's `internal/session/policies.go` /\n38:   `AGENTS.md` are not present in this repository, so the dedupe check in\n39:   TASK-6 is limited to the files that actually exist here.\n40: \n41: ## Task breakdown\n42: \n43: ### TASK-1 — Author `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n44: \n45: - **Description**: Create the global policy file forbidding committing,\n46:   logging, printing or hardcoding secrets, tokens, keys or credentials\n47:   (read them from env/config instead), written as a short universal\n48:   always/never rule per the brief's format.\n49: - **Files**: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` (new)\n50: - **Depends**: none\n51: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file, no code paths or other artifacts\n52:   affected.\n53: \n54: ### TASK-2 — Author `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n55: \n56: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no debug\n57:   output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO (without a tracked\n58:   issue) be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n59: - **Files**: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` (new)\n60: - **Depends**: none\n61: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n62: \n63: ### TASK-3 — Author `policies/smallest-change.md`\n64: \n65: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring the smallest change\n66:   that satisfies the task (no refactoring or tidying of adjacent code, no scope\n67:   expansion), framed as a session-wide constraint rather than a developer-only\n68:   instruction.\n69: - **Files**: `policies/smallest-change.md` (new)\n70: - **Depends**: none\n71: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; the only judgement call is wording to\n72:   avoid merely restating `agents/developer.md` (noted above).\n73: \n74: ### TASK-4 — Author `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n75: \n76: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring explicit approval\n77:   before adding a dependency, framed universally for all sessions/agents.\n78: - **Files**: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` (new)\n79: - **Depends**: none\n80: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; overlaps slightly with the developer\n81:   prompt, so wording must add the session-wide framing.\n82: \n83: ### TASK-5 — Author `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n84: \n85: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no uncommitted\n86:   work be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n87: - **Files**: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` (new)\n88: - **Depends**: none\n89: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n90: \n91: ### TASK-6 — Audit the new `policies/` set against the brief's criteria\n92: \n93: - **Description**: Compare all files under `policies/` against the brief's four\n94:   decision criteria and the existing catalog content that actually exists here\n95:   (`prompts/*.md`, `agents/*.md`, `skills/`); trim wording, or drop a file\n96:   entirely, if it is not universal, is longer than a short rule, restates a\n97:   skill or a core agent prompt with no added scope, or is situational — and\n98:   record any such decision in `implementation.md`.\n99: - **Files**: `policies/*.md` (may be edited or, if a file fails the criteria,\n100:   removed); `implementation.md` (note the outcome)\n101: - **Depends**: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n102: - **Risk**: medium — this is a judgement-based pass that can change or reduce\n103:   the delivered set, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n104:   brief's criteria.\n105: \n106: ## Notes / open questions\n107: \n108: - The brief leaves the exact set open (\"names/content are a starting\n109:   suggestion\"). These tasks author all five proposed policies and rely on\n110:   TASK-6 to enforce the criteria; if a policy fails, the brief's intent is to\n111:   drop it, so the final set may be fewer than five. This is treated as in\n112:   scope, not a scope expansion.\n113: - No human decision was required to produce this breakdown.\n\n(End of file - total 113 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: policies\n\nid: medical\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\nsmall set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\nplain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\nthe four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\nreal spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n\nScope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n  `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: policies\n\nid: medical\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\nsmall set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\nplain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\nthe four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\nreal spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n\nScope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n  `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the\n  brief says keep the directory to policy files only (the catalog scan ignores\n  those, but the brief is explicit).\n- Every file must be short: a one-line heading + the rule + at most a line or\n  two of why. If a rule needs more than that, it belongs in a skill, not here.\n\nNotes for @developer (not blockers):\n- The repo contains no build or test tooling; verification is content review\n  against the brief's criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n- The brief is explicit that names/content are a starting suggestion. Several\n  proposed rules (`smallest-change`, `ask-before-adding-dependencies`,\n  `keep-it-committed`) overlap with existing core agent instructions\n  (`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/developer.md`). Author them as *universal,\n  session-wide* constraints (they apply to every agent, not just the\n  developer), not as a restatement of the developer prompt. If a rule cannot\n  be made meaningfully broader than an existing prompt/skill, flag it in\n  `implementation.md` rather than inventing scope.\n- The brief's `~70 more` skills and manigot's `internal/session/policies.go` /\n  `AGENTS.md` are not present in this repository, so the dedupe check in\n  TASK-6 is limited to the files that actually exist here.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n### TASK-1 — Author `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file forbidding committing,\n  logging, printing or hardcoding secrets, tokens, keys or credentials\n  (read them from env/config instead), written as a short universal\n  always/never rule per the brief's format.\n- **Files**: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file, no code paths or other artifacts\n  affected.\n\n### TASK-2 — Author `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no debug\n  output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO (without a tracked\n  issue) be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n- **Files**: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n\n### TASK-3 — Author `policies/smallest-change.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring the smallest change\n  that satisfies the task (no refactoring or tidying of adjacent code, no scope\n  expansion), framed as a session-wide constraint rather than a developer-only\n  instruction.\n- **Files**: `policies/smallest-change.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; the only judgement call is wording to\n  avoid merely restating `agents/developer.md` (noted above).\n\n### TASK-4 — Author `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring explicit approval\n  before adding a dependency, framed universally for all sessions/agents.\n- **Files**: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; overlaps slightly with the developer\n  prompt, so wording must add the session-wide framing.\n\n### TASK-5 — Author `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no uncommitted\n  work be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n- **Files**: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n\n### TASK-6 — Audit the new `policies/` set against the brief's criteria\n\n- **Description**: Compare all files under `policies/` against the brief's four\n  decision criteria and the existing catalog content that actually exists here\n  (`prompts/*.md`, `agents/*.md`, `skills/`); trim wording, or drop a file\n  entirely, if it is not universal, is longer than a short rule, restates a\n  skill or a core agent prompt with no added scope, or is situational — and\n  record any such decision in `implementation.md`.\n- **Files**: `policies/*.md` (may be edited or, if a file fails the criteria,\n  removed); `implementation.md` (note the outcome)\n- **Depends**: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n- **Risk**: medium — this is a judgement-based pass that can change or reduce\n  the delivered set, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n  brief's criteria.\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- The brief leaves the exact set open (\"names/content are a starting\n  suggestion\"). These tasks author all five proposed policies and rely on\n  TASK-6 to enforce the criteria; if a policy fails, the brief's intent is to\n  drop it, so the final set may be fewer than five. This is treated as in\n  scope, not a scope expansion.\n- No human decision was required to produce this breakdown.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":113,"totalLines":113,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791734038256,"end":1791734038272}},"id":"prt_12babba8c001LaU0YVQw1l6SOG","sessionID":"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21","messageID":"msg_12babaef5001viyOttXGsbIQMK"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791734039554,"sessionID":"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_e02edd81095f44328fd0d11c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/verdict.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/verdict.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Verdict: policies\n2: \n3: id: medical\n4: reviewer: reviewer\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n8: \n9: ## Review\n10: \n11: Branch: `feature/medical_policies` (matches brief). Base: `main` (no\n12: `.manigot/manigot.json` present → fallback). Reviewed via `git diff main...HEAD`.\n13: \n14: TASK-1: PASS\n15: notes: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` present (5 lines: one-line heading +\n16: rule + 2 lines why). Universal, no frontmatter, filename-only identity.\n17: Matches brief wording (never commit/log/print/hardcode secrets; read from\n18: env/config). No always-on rule existed before (only role checklists in\n19: `agents/security.md:70,88,106` and a passing mention in `agents/architect.md`),\n20: so it adds coverage rather than restating an always-on constraint.\n21: \n22: TASK-2: PASS\n23: notes: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` present, short and universal.\n24: Judgement call verified: the wording closely mirrors `agents/quality.md:92`\n25: (\"no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO comments left\n26: without a tracking issue\"). Criterion 3 warns against restating a core agent's\n27: instructions, but that line is role-scoped to the on-demand `quality` review\n28: agent and never reaches other sessions; promoting it to an always-on rule is\n29: genuinely broader. The brief itself lists `no-debug-leftovers` in the proposed\n30: starter set, so keeping it is within the intended latitude. Acceptable.\n31: \n32: TASK-3: PASS\n33: notes: `policies/smallest-change.md` was created (commit 26a6159) then removed\n34: by the TASK-6 audit (commit cd9f132); it is absent from the final diff. This is\n35: the correct outcome and explicitly anticipated by both the brief and tasks.md\n36: (\"the final set may be fewer than five\"). Verified the removal rationale:\n37: `prompts/meta.md:10-11,15` already imposes this session-wide (\"never silently\n38: expand a task\", \"Don't do things you're not asked to do\"), so a catalog policy\n39: would be a pure restatement per criterion 3. No deliverable is missing.\n40: \n41: TASK-4: PASS\n42: notes: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` present, short, framed\n43: session-wide. Only prior coverage is `agents/developer.md:51` (\"Do not install\n44: packages without asking first\"), which is developer-role-only; the policy adds\n45: all-session scope. Passes the dedupe check.\n46: \n47: TASK-5: PASS\n48: notes: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` present, short, universal. Prior\n49: coverage is developer-role-only commit steps in `agents/developer.md`;\n50: `prompts/meta.md` does not cover committing. Adds scope. The\n51: implementation.md caveat (read-only agents have nothing to commit) is honest\n52: and does not undermine the rule.\n53: \n54: TASK-6: PASS\n55: notes: Audit performed and fully recorded in `implementation.md`. Dropped\n56: exactly one file (`smallest-change`) with per-file rationale; kept four. Every\n57: dedupe claim spot-checked against the actual repo and confirmed\n58: (`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/quality.md:92`, `agents/security.md`, \n59: `agents/developer.md:51`). No frontmatter, `README`, hidden files or symlinks\n60: in `policies/` (verified: directory contains exactly the four `.md` files).\n61: \n62: Scope: clean. `git diff main...HEAD --name-only` shows only the four\n63: `policies/*.md` files plus this job's own `docs/jobs/medical_policies/`\n64: artifacts (brief/tasks/implementation/verdict/session.log/tokens.json). No\n65: changes to `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/` or anything else. The\n66: `session.log`/`tokens.json` changes are framework bookkeeping, not developer\n67: edits — not a finding.\n68: \n69: ## Security\n70: \n71: No security findings. `secrets-hygiene.md` is itself a security policy and is\n72: phrased correctly (keep secrets out of source, diffs, command output, error\n73: messages). No secret material introduced.\n74: \n75: ## Overall\n76: \n77: APPROVED\n78: \n79: All six tasks are satisfied and match the brief's format and decision\n80: criteria. Nothing must change before merge. Non-blocking observations only:\n81: \n82: - The TASK-6 dedupe audit was necessarily limited to the content in this\n83:   checkout; the brief's referenced `internal/session/policies.go`, `AGENTS.md`\n84:   and \"~70 more\" skills are not present here. `implementation.md` records this\n85:   caveat, which is the correct handling.\n\n(End of file - total 85 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Verdict: policies\n\nid: medical\nreviewer: reviewer\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nBranch: `feature/medical_policies` (matches brief). Base: `main` (no\n`.manigot/manigot.json` present → fallback). Reviewed via `git diff main...HEAD`.\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` present (5 lines: one-line heading +\nrule + 2 lines why). Universal, no frontmatter, filename-only identity.\nMatches brief wording (never commit/log/print/hardcode secrets; read from\nenv/config). No always-on rule existed before (only role checklists in\n`agents/security.md:70,88,106` and a passing mention in `agents/architect.md`),\nso it adds coverage rather than restating an always-on constraint.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/verdict.md","text":"# Verdict: policies\n\nid: medical\nreviewer: reviewer\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nBranch: `feature/medical_policies` (matches brief). Base: `main` (no\n`.manigot/manigot.json` present → fallback). Reviewed via `git diff main...HEAD`.\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` present (5 lines: one-line heading +\nrule + 2 lines why). Universal, no frontmatter, filename-only identity.\nMatches brief wording (never commit/log/print/hardcode secrets; read from\nenv/config). No always-on rule existed before (only role checklists in\n`agents/security.md:70,88,106` and a passing mention in `agents/architect.md`),\nso it adds coverage rather than restating an always-on constraint.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` present, short and universal.\nJudgement call verified: the wording closely mirrors `agents/quality.md:92`\n(\"no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO comments left\nwithout a tracking issue\"). Criterion 3 warns against restating a core agent's\ninstructions, but that line is role-scoped to the on-demand `quality` review\nagent and never reaches other sessions; promoting it to an always-on rule is\ngenuinely broader. The brief itself lists `no-debug-leftovers` in the proposed\nstarter set, so keeping it is within the intended latitude. Acceptable.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: `policies/smallest-change.md` was created (commit 26a6159) then removed\nby the TASK-6 audit (commit cd9f132); it is absent from the final diff. This is\nthe correct outcome and explicitly anticipated by both the brief and tasks.md\n(\"the final set may be fewer than five\"). Verified the removal rationale:\n`prompts/meta.md:10-11,15` already imposes this session-wide (\"never silently\nexpand a task\", \"Don't do things you're not asked to do\"), so a catalog policy\nwould be a pure restatement per criterion 3. No deliverable is missing.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` present, short, framed\nsession-wide. Only prior coverage is `agents/developer.md:51` (\"Do not install\npackages without asking first\"), which is developer-role-only; the policy adds\nall-session scope. Passes the dedupe check.\n\nTASK-5: PASS\nnotes: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` present, short, universal. Prior\ncoverage is developer-role-only commit steps in `agents/developer.md`;\n`prompts/meta.md` does not cover committing. Adds scope. The\nimplementation.md caveat (read-only agents have nothing to commit) is honest\nand does not undermine the rule.\n\nTASK-6: PASS\nnotes: Audit performed and fully recorded in `implementation.md`. Dropped\nexactly one file (`smallest-change`) with per-file rationale; kept four. Every\ndedupe claim spot-checked against the actual repo and confirmed\n(`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/quality.md:92`, `agents/security.md`, \n`agents/developer.md:51`). No frontmatter, `README`, hidden files or symlinks\nin `policies/` (verified: directory contains exactly the four `.md` files).\n\nScope: clean. `git diff main...HEAD --name-only` shows only the four\n`policies/*.md` files plus this job's own `docs/jobs/medical_policies/`\nartifacts (brief/tasks/implementation/verdict/session.log/tokens.json). No\nchanges to `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/` or anything else. The\n`session.log`/`tokens.json` changes are framework bookkeeping, not developer\nedits — not a finding.\n\n## Security\n\nNo security findings. `secrets-hygiene.md` is itself a security policy and is\nphrased correctly (keep secrets out of source, diffs, command output, error\nmessages). No secret material introduced.\n\n## Overall\n\nAPPROVED\n\nAll six tasks are satisfied and match the brief's format and decision\ncriteria. Nothing must change before merge. Non-blocking observations only:\n\n- The TASK-6 dedupe audit was necessarily limited to the content in this\n  checkout; the brief's referenced `internal/session/policies.go`, `AGENTS.md`\n  and \"~70 more\" skills are not present here. `implementation.md` records this\n  caveat, which is the correct handling.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":85,"totalLines":85,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/verdict.md","time":{"start":1791734039542,"end":1791734039551}},"id":"prt_12babbef5001yKs150V63hbUg1","sessionID":"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21","messageID":"msg_12babaef5001viyOttXGsbIQMK"}}
