fore (only role checklists in\\n`agents/security.md:70,88,106` and a passing mention in `agents/architect.md`),\\nso it adds coverage rather than restating an always-on constraint.\\n\\nTASK-2: PASS\\nnotes: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` present, short and universal.\\nJudgement call verified: the wording closely mirrors `agents/quality.md:92`\\n(\\\"no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO comments left\\nwithout a tracking issue\\\"). Criterion 3 warns against restating a core agent's\\ninstructions, but that line is role-scoped to the on-demand `quality` review\\nagent and never reaches other sessions; promoting it to an always-on rule is\\ngenuinely broader. The brief itself lists `no-debug-leftovers` in the proposed\\nstarter set, so keeping it is within the intended latitude. Acceptable.\\n\\nTASK-3: PASS\\nnotes: `policies/smallest-change.md` was created (commit 26a6159) then removed\\nby the TASK-6 audit (commit cd9f132); it is absent from the final diff. This is\\nthe correct outcome and explicitly anticipated by both the brief and tasks.md\\n(\\\"the final set may be fewer than five\\\"). Verified the removal rationale:\\n`prompts/meta.md:10-11,15` already imposes this session-wide (\\\"never silently\\nexpand a task\\\", \\\"Don't do things you're not asked to do\\\"), so a catalog policy\\nwould be a pure restatement per criterion 3. No deliverable is missing.\\n\\nTASK-4: PASS\\nnotes: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` present, short, framed\\nsession-wide. Only prior coverage is `agents/developer.md:51` (\\\"Do not install\\npackages without asking first\\\"), which is developer-role-only; the policy adds\\nall-session scope. Passes the dedupe check.\\n\\nTASK-5: PASS\\nnotes: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` present, short, universal. Prior\\ncoverage is developer-role-only commit steps in `agents/developer.md`;\\n`prompts/meta.md` does not cover committing. Adds scope. The\\nimplementation.md caveat (read-only agents have nothing to commit) is honest\\nand does not undermine the rule.\\n\\nTASK-6: PASS\\nnotes: Audit performed and fully recorded in `implementation.md`. Dropped\\nexactly one file (`smallest-change`) with per-file rationale; kept four. Every\\ndedupe claim spot-checked against the actual repo and confirmed\\n(`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/quality.md:92`, `agents/security.md`, \\n`agents/developer.md:51`). No frontmatter, `README`, hidden files or symlinks\\nin `policies/` (verified: directory contains exactly the four `.md` files).\\n\\nScope: clean. `git diff main...HEAD --name-only` shows only the four\\n`policies/*.md` files plus this job's own `docs/jobs/medical_policies/`\\nartifacts (brief/tasks/implementation/verdict/session.log/tokens.json). No\\nchanges to `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/` or anything else. The\\n`session.log`/`tokens.json` changes are framework bookkeeping, not developer\\nedits — not a finding.\\n\\n## Security\\n\\nNo security findings. `secrets-hygiene.md` is itself a security policy and is\\nphrased correctly (keep secrets out of source, diffs, command output, error\\nmessages). No secret material introduced.\\n\\n## Overall\\n\\nAPPROVED\\n\\nAll six tasks are satisfied and match the brief's format and decision\\ncriteria. Nothing must change before merge. Non-blocking observations only:\\n\\n- The TASK-6 dedupe audit was necessarily limited to the content in this\\n  checkout; the brief's referenced `internal/session/policies.go`, `AGENTS.md`\\n  and \\\"~70 more\\\" skills are not present here. `implementation.md` records this\\n  caveat, which is the correct handling.\",\"lineStart\":1,\"lineEnd\":85,\"totalLines\":85,\"truncated\":false}},\"title\":\"docs/jobs/archive/medical_policies/verdict.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791734039542,\"end\":1791734039551}},\"id\":\"prt_12babbef5001yKs150V63hbUg1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21\",\"messageID\":\"msg_12babaef5001viyOttXGsbIQMK\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791734039852,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_12babb8de001lBA7Rr4rwFJkNw\",\"messageID\":\"msg_12babaef5001viyOttXGsbIQMK\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The `policies/` directory has exactly 5 entries, no hidden files. The new policy's shape matches the siblings (heading + rule + why, ~5 lines). Let me check the medical_policies archive for the format precedent/criteria the tasks reference.\\n\\n\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791734036702,\"end\":1791734039844}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791734039947,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_12babc579001HbuO7Qd4Yc6IPo\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_12babaef5001viyOttXGsbIQMK\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed455c351ffePunCilhy6Dmx21\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":48888,\"input\":528,\"output\":232,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":48128}},\"cost\":0.000362784}}\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/tasks.md b/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/tasks.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0fcb9e2\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/tasks.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@\n+# Tasks: new policy: playwright only if necessary\n+\n+id: prior\n+analyst: analyst\n+date: 2026-10-11\n+\n+<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Add one new global catalog policy under `policies/` capturing the brief's rule:\n+browser automation (Playwright, and the `shot` render path that drives it) is\n+expensive, so it should be reached for only when it is genuinely necessary or\n+helpful — static analysis and cheaper verification come first. This is a\n+content-only change: a single plain-markdown policy file, no frontmatter,\n+following the format the `medical_policies` job established (one-line heading +\n+the rule + at most a line or two of why; the filename is the identity).\n+\n+Scope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n+- The deliverable is a **global catalog policy** at `policies/<name>.md` — the\n+  brief says \"create a new policy\", and this repo's source-of-truth policy\n+  directory is the top-level `policies/` (not `docs/policies/`, which is the\n+  per-project tier described in `docs/AGENTS.md`).\n+- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n+  `docs/` other than this job's own files.\n+- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — keep\n+  the directory to policy files only.\n+- Keep the file short: heading + rule + at most a line or two of why.\n+\n+## Framing note for @developer (important, not a blocker)\n+\n+The `medical_policies` brief's decision criteria for a global catalog policy\n+are the real format spec here: a policy must be **universal** (true for every\n+project/language/task) and must **not be situational or tool-specific** — if a\n+rule is \"when doing X, …\", it belongs in a **skill** or a **project** policy,\n+never a global catalog one. A rule named purely after one tool (`playwright`)\n+reads as situational and would fail criterion 1/4.\n+\n+Recommended resolution: frame the policy around the **universal principle** —\n+prefer the cheapest sufficient verification; reserve slow/heavyweight tooling\n+(browser automation such as Playwright, or `shot` renders) for when static\n+analysis, reading the code, or lighter tests genuinely cannot answer the\n+question — and name Playwright as the concrete motivating example rather than\n+the whole subject. Suggested filename: `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md`\n+(the filename is the policy's identity and should stay recognisable).\n+\n+Known tension to record (do **not** silently expand scope): `agents/developer.md`\n+lines ~107-129 instruct the developer to verify UI changes with `shot`, and\n+`agents/tester.md` line ~96 points at the `webapp-testing` skill (Playwright).\n+The policy must **complement** those role instructions, not contradict them;\n+word it so it governs *when* to reach for the browser, leaving the existing\n+\"verify rendered UI work\" guidance intact. If a genuine contradiction cannot be\n+avoided without editing an agent file, stop and flag it in `implementation.md`\n+rather than editing `agents/` (that is out of scope for this brief).\n+\n+## Task breakdown\n+\n+### TASK-1 — Author `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file carrying the brief's rule —\n+  browser automation / Playwright is a costly verification path, so use it only\n+  when it is strictly necessary or genuinely helpful; prefer static analysis and\n+  cheaper checks first. Write it as a short, universal, session-wide always/\n+  never constraint (heading + rule + a line of why), tool-neutral in spirit with\n+  Playwright named only as the motivating example.\n+- **Files**: `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only; the only judgement call is the\n+  universal framing (see note above), not any code path.\n+\n+### TASK-2 — Audit the new policy against the existing catalog\n+\n+- **Description**: Check the new file against the `medical_policies` criteria\n+  and the catalog content that actually exists here: shorten wording if it\n+  exceeds a short rule, and confirm it (a) is universal, (b) adds scope rather\n+  than restating the `webapp-testing`/`frontend-design` skills or\n+  `prompts/meta.md`, and (c) does not contradict `agents/developer.md` (the\n+  `shot` render guidance) or `agents/tester.md` (Playwright via\n+  `webapp-testing`). Adjust the phrasing to resolve any conflict within the\n+  policy file; record the dedupe/consistency reasoning and any decision that\n+  cannot be made in-file in `implementation.md`.\n+- **Files**: `policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md` (may be edited);\n+  `implementation.md` (record the outcome)\n+- **Depends**: TASK-1\n+- **Risk**: medium — a judgement-based pass that can change or trim the\n+  delivered wording, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n+  brief's criteria and the \"add scope, don't restate\" rule.\n+\n+## Notes / open questions\n+\n+- The brief's `Why`, `Out of scope`, and `Notes` sections are empty; the What is\n+  specific enough to proceed. No human decision was required. The main open\n+  design point — universal-principle framing vs. a Playwright-named rule — is\n+  resolved in favour of the universal framing above, because a situational rule\n+  does not qualify as a global catalog policy; if the reviewer disagrees, the\n+  alternative is a `docs/policies/` project rule or a skill, which is a larger\n+  decision than this brief describes.\n+- This repo has no build/test tooling; verification is content review against\n+  the policy format and criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n+- If a follow-up is ever wanted (e.g. softening `agents/developer.md`'s\n+  unconditional \"verify UI with shot\" wording), it is out of scope here and\n+  should be tracked as its own job.\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/tokens.json b/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/tokens.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..ed5bdf0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/tokens.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"agent\": \"analyst\",\n+    \"attempt\": 1,\n+    \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-11T15:49:40.975015895Z\",\n+    \"inputTokens\": 38434,\n+    \"outputTokens\": 3555,\n+    \"cacheReadTokens\": 395264,\n+    \"reasoningTokens\": 3902,\n+    \"costUSD\": 0.011425092\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"agent\": \"developer\",\n+    \"attempt\": 1,\n+    \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-11T15:52:16.543470115Z\",\n+    \"inputTokens\": 74769,\n+    \"outputTokens\": 6028,\n+    \"cacheReadTokens\": 631168,\n+    \"reasoningTokens\": 2695,\n+    \"costUSD\": 0.018342654\n+  }\n+]\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/verdict.md b/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/verdict.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..e88dc6a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/prior_new-policy-playwright-only-if-necessary/verdict.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+# Verdict: new policy: playwright only if necessary\n+\n+id: prior\n+reviewer:\n+date:\n+\n+<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n+\n+## Review\n+\n+<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n+     notes: ...\n+\n+TASK-2: ...\n+-->\n+\n+## Security\n+\n+<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n+\n+## Overall\n+\n+<!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n+<!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->\ndiff --git a/policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md b/policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..b45e327\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/playwright-only-if-necessary.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\n+# Browser automation only if necessary\n+\n+Prefer static analysis, reading the code, or a lighter test over browser\n+automation; reach for Playwright (or a `shot` render) only when those cannot\n+answer the question.\n+Driving a browser is slow and costly, so it should be the exception, not the\n+default.\n","exit":0,"truncated":true,"outputPath":"/home/claude/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_12bacf4db001o7GYvvVJA7Q1dP"},"title":"git diff main...HEAD","time":{"start":1791734117567,"end":1791734117683}},"id":"prt_12bacf41e001Xm0m3GFYTlxk8a","sessionID":"ses_ed4533d96ffeHX0igUlp1xblch","messageID":"msg_12bacea6b001ubNuSJobccoetO"}}
